    "path": "skills/incident-summary/SKILL.md",
    "body": "# Incident Summary Generator\n\nTakes raw incident logs and optional team notes captured during an incident and produces a structured post-incident summary following DBS Platform Engineering's standard template.\n\n## Usage\n\nPaste the relevant log output (error logs, alert payloads, timeline entries) and any notes the on-call team captured. The skill outputs a summary covering timeline, impact, root cause, and action items.\n\n## Inputs\n\n| Input | Type | Required | Notes |\n|-------|------|----------|-------|\n| `logs` | Plain text | Yes | Raw logs, alerts, or monitoring output |\n| `team_notes` | Plain text | No | Slack thread, war-room notes, etc. |\n\n## Example output\n\n```\nPOST-INCIDENT SUMMARY\n=====================\nIncident: API gateway latency spike\nSeverity: P2\nDuration: 2026-04-10 14:32 – 15:07 SGT (35 min)\n\nTIMELINE\n14:32 — PagerDuty alert: p99 latency > 2s on /api/v2/payments\n14:38 — On-call acknowledged; identified upstream DB connection pool exhaustion\n14:55 — Connection pool limit increased; latency recovering\n15:07 — All-clear; latency back to baseline\n\nIMPACT\n~1,200 payment requests degraded; no failures; no data loss.\n\nROOT CAUSE\nDB connection pool capped at 50; traffic spike to 3x normal during promo event.\n\nACTION ITEMS\n- [ ] Raise connection pool limit to 200 (Platform, by 2026-04-17)\n- [ ] Add pool exhaustion alert before latency degrades (Observability, by 2026-04-21)\n```\n\n## Caveats\n\n- Experimental maturity — validate the timeline and root cause carefully before publishing to stakeholders.\n- Do not include customer PII in logs passed to this skill."
